				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/candidkiss" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(459864); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=459864&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608349735" alt="candidkiss" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=459864)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/candidkiss" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(459864); return false;" >candidkiss</a></span> <span class="odate time_1310947253 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">18 Jul 2011 00:00</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1203906">
									

<p>An amazing story. Personally, my favorite bit is when the Foundation agent spoke. To have that much reserve and courage for a child you've never met before, in the face of your own death, really adds a level of character to some of the faceless Foundation personnel.</p>
<p>Although there is the Church of the Broken God, Marshall Carter &amp; Dark, and various other organizations out there, we can't forget that the <strong>Foundation</strong> is extremely powerful, if not more so. I would like to see more stories like this, where unnamed Foundation personnel get their characters flesh out a bit.</p>

							</div>

								
					
